emy-id "q-51148" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{({x}^{2}+4)x}=\\frac{-x+B}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{1}{x},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+4)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & =(-x+B)x+({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)+4 & =(-1+B)(1)+({1}^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =-1+B+5 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51148/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51148"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9be4bc3b-d8c1-5fb7-bf55-a44cff4d2e19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "a54598da-db80-570e-bc72-b2ec2605c1c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cb976e1a-4d18-5df2-912b-205fa9206080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145/selection/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d" :answer/id #uuid "27b7181b-4bbe-5126-b9e0-a4a91d21f801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "3ccdc484-a2d1-561d-944c-fefca31fc474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f584bd85-6233-5282-95a2-1668d08c4511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51145/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-51145/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-51145/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" "q-51145/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-51145/selection/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d" "q-51145/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51145" :question/id #uuid "a495ca31-c4d0-5391-8935-5af67c5a3fbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-51145" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+5}{({x}^{2}+2)(x-1)}=\\frac{2x+B}{{x}^{2}+2}+\\frac{2}{x-1},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+2)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3x+5 & =(2x+B)(x-1)+2({x}^{2}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-3(0)+5 & =(2(0)+B)(0-1)+2({0}^{2}+2) \\\\ 5 & =(B)(-1)+2(2) \\\\ 5 & =-B+4 \\\\ 1 & =-B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51145/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "3690fc1f-4c84-57fa-b606-75788d3e9b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "19ca4568-bc12-5c7f-af12-b55a44d28fac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346957/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-346957/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957/field-2/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "416ace5f-a095-5b1d-9f53-7a89a7595257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b651625-8eef-5707-9a2f-83184ef2d966" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346957/field-2/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-346957/field-2/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "1f03868e-b94d-5f9b-a926-e9c2b6a05ba7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e237352-c2c2-53e3-b6f8-254875dcd5e5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346957/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-346957/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346957" :question/id #uuid "c3fb4ddf-fa1a-5f35-80c1-327fb7940b68" :question/math-academy-id "q-346957" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}}$\\,x\\,+$\n{{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $8({x}^{2}+4)$ |  | $8(x+2)$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{C}{x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)$ gives\n\n$$\n5=(Ax+B)(x+2)+C({x}^{2}+4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =C(4+4) \\\\ 5 & =8C \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(0)+B)(0+2)+\\frac{5}{8}((0)^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =2B+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 2B & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ B & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(1)+\\frac{5}{4})(1+2)+\\frac{5}{8}((1)^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =3A+\\frac{15}{4}+\\frac{25}{8} \\\\ 3A & =-\\frac{15}{8} \\\\ A & =-\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{5}{8}x+\\frac{5}{4})}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{(\\frac{5}{8})}{x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\,x+10}{8({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{5}{8(x+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346957/field-1" "q-346957/field-2" "q-346957/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346957"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1713d332-60d4-591f-bf69-a0913d558295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "f31e57cb-ff1a-5023-b45b-ec9b95bbe2fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "93313f00-9831-50cb-b1ed-d8b81a7a6bb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "77cdba82-3004-56ea-8b64-f3446b0474d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "07cac761-a84c-58c0-8abd-fdcd0a4d9a84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0cda6f27-f7a0-5e96-9b9b-ac67a8a7873f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49723/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-49723/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-49723/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-49723/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-49723/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-49723/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49723" :question/id #uuid "bf64e5dc-bb83-5617-9421-c46540619689" :question/math-academy-id "q-49723" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{C}{x-2},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)$ and get\n\n$$\n7x=(Ax+B)(x-2)+C({x}^{2}+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2) & =(A(2)+B)(2-2)+C({2}^{2}+3) \\\\ 14 & =7C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0) & =(A(0)+B)(0-2)+(2)({0}^{2}+3) \\\\ 0 & =-2B+6 \\\\ 2B & =6 \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1) & =(A(1)+3)(1-2)+(2)({1}^{2}+3) \\\\ 7 & =(A+3)(-1)+8 \\\\ 7 & =-A+5 \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-2,$ $B=3,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\nA+B+C=-2+3+2=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49723/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351277/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "b713cca3-6bb1-5083-89df-5043bdc929c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351277/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b2fe99-b4f1-5432-8630-b03865700d1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351277/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-351277/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351277" :question/id #uuid "50e1546d-baa4-5c16-b41d-ac9aaa5971ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-351277" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{43{x}^{2}+4x+2}{(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{43{x}^{2}+4x+2}{(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)}=\\,$ | $x\\,+\\,${{field-1}} | $+$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $6{x}^{2}+1$ |  | $x-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{43{x}^{2}+4x+2}{(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)}=\\frac{x+B}{6{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{7}{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}43{x}^{2}+4x+2 & =(x+B)(x-1)+7(6{x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}43(0)^{2}+4(0)+2 & =(0+B)(0-1)+7(6(0)^{2}+1) \\\\ 2 & =-B+7 \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{43{x}^{2}+4x+2}{(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)}=\\frac{x+5}{6{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{7}{x-1}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351277/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351277"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015/selection/a88e4d3abbdec0a8fd339ecfb4709b7e9c6f3b51e41626ddb1d8f4701cfa5a9a" :answer/id #uuid "dab86164-5e86-582f-a790-f4f2d111cc7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{6}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015/selection/b47543de35b6382933a7033f430cf6949d78ed40053c7f8523960082724f1643" :answer/id #uuid "ffed33a2-8876-5902-a220-7a3b0930283a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{3}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015/selection/452f51d28a4e8fb6a570afc770dff46f9f24a2a1304539f49aa5baaccaeea068" :answer/id #uuid "246a9b61-0e8a-5a21-b8d8-06264175159d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5x-3}{({x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{2}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015/selection/5c8f49db72dd3548046270e243df490395b39ee30243bc88d212d87a7e14c980" :answer/id #uuid "4f394579-1cbf-5a79-aef6-28430d55ca21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-8}{({x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{5}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015/selection/c3c9b3447fe6dfa3d49485d6bbe822c0d80eab1a655b2f67cc4732ae3cea2dda" :answer/id #uuid "a41682cd-77eb-5199-9a83-a429790912b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x+2}{({x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8615af00-5ca7-54d3-a212-9aa564da9141" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11015/selection/452f51d28a4e8fb6a570afc770dff46f9f24a2a1304539f49aa5baaccaeea068" :answer-field/choices ["q-11015/selection/a88e4d3abbdec0a8fd339ecfb4709b7e9c6f3b51e41626ddb1d8f4701cfa5a9a" "q-11015/selection/b47543de35b6382933a7033f430cf6949d78ed40053c7f8523960082724f1643" "q-11015/selection/452f51d28a4e8fb6a570afc770dff46f9f24a2a1304539f49aa5baaccaeea068" "q-11015/selection/5c8f49db72dd3548046270e243df490395b39ee30243bc88d212d87a7e14c980" "q-11015/selection/c3c9b3447fe6dfa3d49485d6bbe822c0d80eab1a655b2f67cc4732ae3cea2dda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11015" :question/id #uuid "0ba96632-d869-56e1-a1ef-bc4e5fea1ab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-11015" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-28x+17}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-28x+17}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-5)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{C}{(x-5)}.\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+1$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+1)(x-5)$ and get\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-28x+17=(Ax+B)(x-5)+C({x}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=5$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(5)^{2}-28(5)+17 & =(A(5)+B)(5-5)+C({5}^{2}+1) \\\\ 175-140+17 & =26C \\\\ 52 & =26C \\\\ C & =\\frac{52}{26} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-28(0)+17 & =(A(0)+B)(0-5)+C({0}^{2}+1) \\\\ 17 & =-5B+C \\\\ 17 & =-5B+2 \\\\ 5B & =2-17 \\\\ B & =-\\frac{15}{5} \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1)^{2}-28(1)+17 & =(A(1)+B)(1-5)+C({1}^{2}+1) \\\\ -4 & =-4A-4B+2C \\\\ -4 & =-4A-4(-3)+2(2) \\\\ 4A & =12+4+4 \\\\ A & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=5,$ $B=-3,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-28x+17}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-5)}=\\frac{5x-3}{({x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{2}{(x-5)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11015/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561/selection/c9d5436f050a5ac3d5a891aff0cb16886232d14fc6b92675c0678c7fc06f7549" :answer/id #uuid "4242797a-4904-585e-80e9-32b186ba1f10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561/selection/b8379365cf4893565bfb3d056bca9f2744e45da6ea88954ca4dd5249c2a9c125" :answer/id #uuid "b43fd6df-ac80-58f7-b04d-6a75e53f78af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x-5}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561/selection/bd36e3bda3647d6a664d9890622680411000f34b409c0a5f606d38e3dd29fd20" :answer/id #uuid "9a20ffb8-6d84-58b9-aaad-4aa88f241da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561/selection/1c696185d7188338e75ad2d0b534179d2bb26ebda9433a8e160d26e421a7b879" :answer/id #uuid "2ad8c427-9061-5d56-96b7-aaf7ea7df328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561/selection/e361342899728d0cc4bd9dea1e5b549d7baaf8e47c72591ca04fdb705d2f3ebb" :answer/id #uuid "1cdbff02-3dae-518a-b942-37e882a23c3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-4}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{5}{(x+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f2d2ec3-c0fa-51a0-b5be-8d3b2b96ece2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102561/selection/c9d5436f050a5ac3d5a891aff0cb16886232d14fc6b92675c0678c7fc06f7549" :answer-field/choices ["q-102561/selection/c9d5436f050a5ac3d5a891aff0cb16886232d14fc6b92675c0678c7fc06f7549" "q-102561/selection/b8379365cf4893565bfb3d056bca9f2744e45da6ea88954ca4dd5249c2a9c125" "q-102561/selection/bd36e3bda3647d6a664d9890622680411000f34b409c0a5f606d38e3dd29fd20" "q-102561/selection/1c696185d7188338e75ad2d0b534179d2bb26ebda9433a8e160d26e421a7b879" "q-102561/selection/e361342899728d0cc4bd9dea1e5b549d7baaf8e47c72591ca04fdb705d2f3ebb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102561" :question/id #uuid "10213766-0256-5950-8424-1b014b86c8e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-102561" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x-3}{({x}^{2}+6)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x-3}{({x}^{2}+6)(x+5)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+6$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+6)(x+5)$ and get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+2x-3=(Ax+B)(x+5)+C({x}^{2}+6).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-5$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-5)^{2}+2(-5)-3 & =(A(-5)+B)(-5+5)+C((-5)^{2}+6) \\\\ 75-10-3 & =31C \\\\ C & =\\frac{62}{31} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}+2(0)-3 & =(A(0)+B)(0+5)+C((0)^{2}+6) \\\\ -3 & =5B+6C \\\\ -3 & =5B+6(2) \\\\ 5B & =-3-12 \\\\ B & =\\frac{-15}{5} \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A$ we choose $x=1$, and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}+2(1)-3 & =(A(1)+B)(1+5)+C((1)^{2}+6) \\\\ 2 & =6A+6B+7C \\\\ 2 & =6A+6(-3)+7(2) \\\\ 6A & =2+18-14 \\\\ A & =\\frac{6}{6} \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=1,B=-3,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x-3}{({x}^{2}+6)(x+5)}=\\frac{x-3}{({x}^{2}+6)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102561/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000/selection/a6ab245daaf60a5908f9c8115d09aa9d50de496c7ce29b5fca04574626d630d2" :answer/id #uuid "988485f1-78d4-5f96-933b-e0321a237844" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000/selection/aa2e1bbe5690ce09502f4d2ee4165c328a816e2677f08b9a87032a412ebde9b7" :answer/id #uuid "de278ca4-78da-5edb-809f-bb893cb8d692" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{4}{(x-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000/selection/b0be2067efad803fdd6af20606dd2b86b9a6cb3fbd11aed60bb34d13f17ef71e" :answer/id #uuid "9bc33aed-910f-542d-89a5-e3b9b93d9eff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000/selection/7cde847d74a0dc1111da3bc4c8f698ba10c32e00c352f1bc3fb540b570f9a16a" :answer/id #uuid "344b7faf-5dc5-5997-9d98-b47327a2de03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{3}{(x-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000/selection/2980a3cef9f2ff50de3caf788d241b1f4cb3c8a760467985089ab34b11319609" :answer/id #uuid "2dadd1bc-6e62-5df1-aa96-345cfbf16446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{5}{(x-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bbd6bfd-645d-5d9f-a3f7-cc2dca25c75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11000/selection/b0be2067efad803fdd6af20606dd2b86b9a6cb3fbd11aed60bb34d13f17ef71e" :answer-field/choices ["q-11000/selection/a6ab245daaf60a5908f9c8115d09aa9d50de496c7ce29b5fca04574626d630d2" "q-11000/selection/aa2e1bbe5690ce09502f4d2ee4165c328a816e2677f08b9a87032a412ebde9b7" "q-11000/selection/b0be2067efad803fdd6af20606dd2b86b9a6cb3fbd11aed60bb34d13f17ef71e" "q-11000/selection/7cde847d74a0dc1111da3bc4c8f698ba10c32e00c352f1bc3fb540b570f9a16a" "q-11000/selection/2980a3cef9f2ff50de3caf788d241b1f4cb3c8a760467985089ab34b11319609"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11000" :question/id #uuid "79d6f845-0357-59f6-a764-58bacb7343f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-11000" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)$ and get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-3x+1=(Ax+B)(x-2)+C({x}^{2}+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)^{2}-3(2)+1 & =(A(2)+B)(2-2)+C({2}^{2}+3) \\\\ 12-6+1 & =7C \\\\ C & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}-3(0)+1 & =(A(0)+B)(0-2)+C({0}^{2}+3) \\\\ 1 & =-2B+3C \\\\ 1 & =-2B+3(1) \\\\ 2B & =2 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}-3(1)+1 & =(A(1)+B)(1-2)+C({1}^{2}+3) \\\\ 1 & =-A-B+4C \\\\ 1 & =-A-1+4(1) \\\\ A & =3-1 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=2,$ $B=1$ and $C=1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}=\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11000/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11000"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571/selection/c61f419ffb50c3ab3ee3d5adaa51c530d2bb5106544f5e1cbd6dce5394aa0626" :answer/id #uuid "839b55c6-fc4e-5ad6-95c6-3cf935cf1aec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{4}{(x+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571/selection/fe7208b32a607e17da1662db60e4db3650f27b9f50fe704ee057a425ff03a56c" :answer/id #uuid "4a1a487b-0945-5763-9900-6ef6b3dc84ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{3}{(x+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571/selection/2bd0f44e4c8d199520c052c5ab21361d2ff541d90730229f230438bafde2bb64" :answer/id #uuid "3efc7843-83ed-5cc9-b8c9-8c21740ac355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x+1}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571/selection/6bece3cd3ac7253436a694497c11c61066bed8b517e988ff1b2a9535112f2c72" :answer/id #uuid "6109b408-7f02-59ea-9026-db2611af7fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571/selection/9c83d2a7e0963c9e5a0431a882c39a7d5ab1f57e06e455a1e86c4c598d4f7960" :answer/id #uuid "7ce9a9fb-acf0-50fb-af75-dd21d1b28e6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x+2}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ca5f77f-0e5e-5977-831a-e0ee2be1f158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102571/selection/9c83d2a7e0963c9e5a0431a882c39a7d5ab1f57e06e455a1e86c4c598d4f7960" :answer-field/choices ["q-102571/selection/c61f419ffb50c3ab3ee3d5adaa51c530d2bb5106544f5e1cbd6dce5394aa0626" "q-102571/selection/fe7208b32a607e17da1662db60e4db3650f27b9f50fe704ee057a425ff03a56c" "q-102571/selection/2bd0f44e4c8d199520c052c5ab21361d2ff541d90730229f230438bafde2bb64" "q-102571/selection/6bece3cd3ac7253436a694497c11c61066bed8b517e988ff1b2a9535112f2c72" "q-102571/selection/9c83d2a7e0963c9e5a0431a882c39a7d5ab1f57e06e455a1e86c4c598d4f7960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102571" :question/id #uuid "4c1cb942-5e45-505d-a155-c6b698d52afc" :question/math-academy-id "q-102571" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-1}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-1}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}-2x+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)$ and get\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+7x-1=(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}-2x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}+7(-1)-1 & =(A(-1)+B)(-1+1)+C((-1)^{2}-2(-1)+3) \\\\ -6 & =6C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)^{2}+7(0)-1 & =(A(0)+B)(0+1)+C({0}^{2}-2(0)+3) \\\\ -1 & =B+3C \\\\ -1 & =B+3(-1) \\\\ B & =3-1 \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)^{2}+7(1)-1 & =(A(1)+B)(1+1)+C((1)^{2}-2(1)+3) \\\\ 8 & =2A+2B+2C \\\\ 8 & =2A+2(2)+2(-1) \\\\ 2A & =8-4+2 \\\\ A & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,B=2,$ and $C=-1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-1}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{3x+2}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011/selection/96247440138440bb2335efd6f9e3ece25f6d89e35d5b20538392b2f088f6ace4" :answer/id #uuid "27742666-28f3-58cd-b003-319d62232e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011/selection/9ba0eba8b9daf13ab9f317487d270ac194e82e2f7fb8a47785176af60a53e16e" :answer/id #uuid "758425cf-afcf-5db3-b667-ada7d202b9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)}-\\frac{6}{(x-6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011/selection/af408ecb33e4a90c9669447e7ff7f7307c2676b7ade89e52ab3f83c497431304" :answer/id #uuid "86ea9850-be63-5094-b0b0-2974518697ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{({x}^{2}+4)}-\\frac{5}{(x-6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011/selection/0f31d3ec51b4b97aadaa4f52cb1384b1492d678917ae01b27ff3f45787519094" :answer/id #uuid "6e389b89-39bf-516b-b0ce-bb9db76cd2c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x-6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011/selection/59a834e7a7b42f56f296e6f63ef18deaf078f06932d003adfa96379191606303" :answer/id #uuid "4c0359a2-8e98-5be3-8f1c-39f1bcc0b91e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{4}{(x-6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0190aaf0-b5a9-5083-a8f9-fda359b7c32b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11011/selection/59a834e7a7b42f56f296e6f63ef18deaf078f06932d003adfa96379191606303" :answer-field/choices ["q-11011/selection/96247440138440bb2335efd6f9e3ece25f6d89e35d5b20538392b2f088f6ace4" "q-11011/selection/9ba0eba8b9daf13ab9f317487d270ac194e82e2f7fb8a47785176af60a53e16e" "q-11011/selection/af408ecb33e4a90c9669447e7ff7f7307c2676b7ade89e52ab3f83c497431304" "q-11011/selection/0f31d3ec51b4b97aadaa4f52cb1384b1492d678917ae01b27ff3f45787519094" "q-11011/selection/59a834e7a7b42f56f296e6f63ef18deaf078f06932d003adfa96379191606303"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11011" :question/id #uuid "e56267e6-e620-5002-b89f-3d6967bcd17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-11011" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+16}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-6)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+16}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-6)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{C}{(x-6)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+4$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+4)(x-6)$ and get\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-18x+16=(Ax+B)(x-6)+C({x}^{2}+4).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=6$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(6)^{2}-18(6)+16 & =(A(6)+B)(6-6)+C({6}^{2}+4) \\\\ 252-108+16 & =40C \\\\ C & =\\frac{160}{40} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-18(0)+16 & =(A(0)+B)(0-6)+C({0}^{2}+4) \\\\ 16 & =-6B+4C \\\\ 16 & =-6B+4(4) \\\\ 6B & =16-16 \\\\ B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1)^{2}-18(1)+16 & =(A(1)+B)(1-6)+C({1}^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =-5A-5B+5C \\\\ 5 & =-5A-5(0)+5(4) \\\\ 5A & =20-5 \\\\ A & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,$ $B=0,$ and $C=4.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+16}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-6)}=\\frac{3x}{({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{4}{(x-6)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11011/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
